 ("Rule 10", "Steam tables, the Mollier diagram, water property diagrams, and the steam cycle are on pages tagged Water-system only, as approved in the manifest review. The user decided on Nov 5, 2026 to remove worked examples tied to PWR or BWR reactor coolant systems.", 41),
 ("User decision", "Examples 2 to 5 of the First Law chapter (primary fluid through a steam generator, reactor coolant pump, reactor core balance, overall primary balance) are left off because they describe a water reactor coolant system.", 63),
 ("Handbook error", "p.21 says Q = mcp∆T is used to calculate latent heat, but p.20 and p.63 show it applies to sensible heat, since ∆T = 0 during a phase change. The lesson uses p.63.", 21),
 ("Handbook error", "p.99 and p.102 say a gas may be treated as incompressible when its velocity is greater than one-third of the speed of sound. This looks reversed, and no approved source settles it. The lesson teaches only the liquid case, and no check tests the gas case.", 99),
 ("Handbook error", "p.50 gives the units of specific volume as lbm/ft³ and uses 1.14162 as both νg and νfg. The worked example here uses enthalpy and entropy only.", 50),
 ("Handbook inconsistency", "The critical pressure is 3206.2 psia on p.36 and 3208.2 psi on p.48. The lesson shows p.36 only, on a tagged page, and no check tests it.", 36),
 ("Handbook inconsistency", "The maximum source temperature is 1960 °R on p.84 and 1962 °R on p.85. The lesson uses neither.", 84),
 ("Handbook error", "Example 5 on p.66 converts 1.0 x 10⁷ Btu/hr to 4007 hp, but 1 hp = 2545 Btu/hr on p.64 gives about 3929 hp. The example is left off.", 66),
 ("Handbook wording", "p.100 refers to Equations 1-44 and 1-45 in a way that does not match their use. The lesson shows the two work equations only.", 100),
 ("Duplicate", "Thermo Units and Properties.docx matches Thermodynamic Units and Properties.docx in every line but the title, so the second file is the base and nothing needs a separate cite.", W(U, "1.2 Terminal Learning Objectives")),
 ("Word claim", "Thermodynamics.docx slide 1.17 says the General Energy Equation is another term for Bernoulli's Equation and is sometimes called the Continuity Equation. The handbooks treat these as different equations, so the claim is left off.", W(TD, "1.17 General Energy Equation")),
 ("Word value", "Word files use practical values of 15 psi and 30 inHg for atmosphere and give the entropy reference as 32.02 °F. These round the handbook's 14.7 psi and 29.9 inHg, and differ from its 32 °F. The lesson uses the handbook.", W(U, "1.27 Comparing Pressure Scales")),
 ("Word source", PICTURES + " The reactor, IHX, and PSP process slides are pictures, so their numbers are not used.", W(TD, "1.28 Reactor Process")),
